      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Utuado is nicknamed “La Ciudad del Viví” after the viví bird, a local symbol of the region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.trawellino.com/destinations/puerto-rico/utuado_utuado",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Perched in Puerto Rico’s Cordillera Central, Utuado is the island’s third‑largest municipality by land area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Utuado%2C_Puerto_Rico",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The University of Puerto Rico at Utuado, founded in 1979, specializes in agricultural studies such as pest control and horticulture.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Utuado%2C_Puerto_Rico",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Caguana Ceremonial Park, a National Historic Landmark in Utuado, preserves the ancient Taíno ceremonial site.",
